From 1a16451f275baf14ede53b5bcdbe84b15a2f4052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:44:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 112/116] ChopGimp: Photoshop-like GimpSpinScale (label, thin
 track with round knob, value field + unit)

GimpSpinScale itself is improved, so filter / layer-style dialogs, tool
options, the layers panel and Python plug-ins all get it:
- label on the left (ellipsized, label column ~30 % of the width so the
  tracks of stacked sliders line up), thin track with filled part and
  round knob, the entry text framed as a small value field, optional
  "unit-suffix" property drawn after it (set automatically: factor 100
  -> "%", GEGL unit degree/pixel/kelvin, brush size/angle, layers
  panel opacity);
- click/drag on the track = absolute value (gamma, scale limits, Ctrl
  page steps, constrain-drag as before), drag on the label = scrub,
  Shift+drag or right button = fine relative drag (TARGET_RELATIVE),
  first click in the field selects the value, Enter / Escape /
  focus-out, wheel and arrows unchanged;
- the -/+ buttons get no width (structural CSS) and their input
  windows are hidden;
- narrow widgets: label over a thinner track, then field only;
- colors and sizes from the theme (.chopgimp-slider-track/-fill/-knob/
  -field/-unit), neutral defaults for other themes.
CHOPGIMP_CLASSIC_SPIN_SCALE=1 restores the classic filled bar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
